Totality Chivaree
Ingredients: SKA + EUPHORIC, ENERGETIC & JOLLY + Harpsichord
Creative Catalyst: Born from itinerant midway buskers who only strike an instrument when the moon swallows the midday sun, turning sudden daytime darkness into frantic, golden joy.

Totality Chivaree sounds like an 18th-century royal court thrown down an active carnival midway at 160 beats per minute. Frantic, double-plucked French harpsichord arpeggios replace the standard ska guitar skank, locking directly into athletic upright slap-bass lines and explosive brass-band fanfares. It is delirium dressed in powdered wigs and clown greasepaint: ecstatic, bright, and dangerously kinetic, radiating the manic relief of musicians trying to play an entire festival's worth of dancing into the four brief minutes of an astronomical blackout.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 148–168 BPM. An unyielding, caffeinated two-step skank rooted in the offbeat, driven by the snap of harpsichord plectrums on the "and" of every beat while a marching bass drum drives the downbeat.
- Harmonic Palette: Sparkling D Major, G Lydian, and celebratory Baroque Picardy thirds; sudden, theatrical chromatic modulations that mimic the erratic corona flares of the eclipsed sun.
- Production Signatures: 
  1. Plectrum-Gating: Close-miking antique harpsichord jacks with contact microphones run through sidechained noise gates triggered by the kick drum, turning delicate keyboard quills into percussive, chopping weaponry.
  2. Corona-Bloom Reverb: Chamber plates automated to explode into massive, shimmering sixty-foot spatial reverbs specifically during brass breaks, simulating the acoustic shock of sudden atmospheric temperature drops.
  3. Calliope Rotary Bleed: Running trumpet and trombone stems through motorized Leslie speakers and antique steam-organ baffles to give the brass an authentic, dizzying carousel swirl.
- Dynamics: The music operates with zero patience: it ignites instantaneously at peak volume, surges through hyperactive horn refrains, drops into a breathless two-bar harpsichord solo during simulated "totality," then violently explodes back into maximum carnival pandemonium.

Scene & Origin Lore
The subculture surfaced along the shifting, zigzagging "Paths of Totality"—the geographic ribbons where complete solar eclipses touch earth. Troupes known as Chivaristes travel in painted steam wagons year-round, tracking celestial calculations and refusing to play a single rehearsal note in direct sunlight. When the sky darkens at noon, they erupt into the streets wearing harlequin ruffs, soot-blackened prism goggles, and frock coats stitched from discarded circus banners. The scene developed its own fast-talking carny cant called Karnavolo, characterized by frantic group chants, backflips off harpsichord lids, and crowds violently skanking in circle-pits while tossing golden foil confetti toward the blacked-out sky. To a Chivariste, daylight is a boring waiting room; only the sun’s temporary death earns their ecstatic racket.

Typical Instruments: Two-manual Flemish Harpsichord (double-strung and contact-mic'd), Upright Slap Bass, Marching Snare, Valve Trombone, Tenor Saxophone, B-flat Cornet, Mechanical Calliope Organ, Field Tambourine.

